{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18499 - PROTEIN:1381",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that gamma-Glutamylhistidine may interact with Beclin-1 through multiple indirect pathways. The molecule is identified as a target of several compounds, including N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide and Spongia-13(16),14-Dien-19-Oic Acid, both of which are predicted to target Beclin-1. Additionally, gamma-Glutamylhistidine is also linked to ATP synthase subunit a, which is a target of Puqiedine, another compound that targets Beclin-1. These findings collectively indicate that gamma-Glutamylhistidine may influence Beclin-1 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving enzyme activity or signaling pathways. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role for gamma-Glutamylhistidine in modulating Beclin-1 function, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
